@@ -1130,6 +1130,53 @@
         { "a": "NewZealand", "b": "USSR", "value": 15.0 },
         { "a": "NewZealand", "b": "France", "value": -30.0 }
       ]
+    },
+    {
+      "note": [
+        "West Africa (branch feat/r2-westafrica2). Eleven nations were added to the roster with exactly one territorial claim between them, which is the transcribed fact and would leave the region looking placid. It was not placid. What these states did to each other in 1990 was sponsor each other's rebels, close each other's borders and expel each other's populations, and this block is where that goes - it is the half of the region's politics that adjacency and claims cannot carry.",
+        "Senegal and Mauritania at -55 is the lowest number in this block and one of the lowest in the file, and it is fifteen months old when the game opens. A quarrel between Soninke farmers and Mauritanian herders at Diawara on 9 April 1989 killed two men; within a week there were pogroms against Mauritanian shopkeepers in Dakar and against black Africans in Nouakchott, several hundred dead on both sides, and by the end of the summer something like 70,000 people had been airlifted or driven across the river in each direction. Mauritania used the crisis to expel tens of thousands of its own Halpulaar and Soninke citizens as Senegalese. Diplomatic relations were broken off in August 1989 and were not restored until April 1992. Two states with a border, a river, an argument about whose people are whose, and no shooting war - which is exactly the state a relations number has to be able to hold when there is no claim to explain it.",
+        "Liberia's row is the war. On 24 December 1989 Charles Taylor crossed into Nimba County from Cote d'Ivoire with fighters trained at Tajura in Libya and staged through Burkina Faso, and Ouagadougou's involvement was not deniable: Blaise Compaore supplied men and a transit route and had been Taylor's patron since Taylor walked out of a Ghanaian jail. Liberia-Burkina Faso at -45 and Liberia-Libya at -50 are that. Against them, Samuel Doe's friends: the United States, which had put something like half a billion dollars into Liberia in the 1980s for a Voice of America relay, an Omega navigation station and a CIA station, and which by January 1990 was quietly done with him; Israel, whose relations Doe restored in 1983 as the first African state to break the post-1973 boycott; and Nigeria, whose Ibrahim Babangida was personally close to Doe and who eight months later put the largest contingent into ECOMOG to stop Taylor taking Monrovia.",
+        "Ghana and Togo at -30 is the quarrel the roster's Togo row declines to enter as a claim. There is a real irredentism underneath it - Ewe reunification and the western half of former German Togoland, which is now Ghana's Volta region - but by 1990 what the two governments actually did was accuse each other of coups: Lome blamed Accra and Ouagadougou for the commando raid on Lome of 23 September 1986, Accra blamed Lome for hosting its dissidents, and the border shut and reopened for a decade. A hostility with no territorial demand behind it, which is what this table is for.",
+        "France's numbers are the franc zone, and they are not uniform. Togo at 55 and Niger at 55 are the two Paris cared most about keeping - Eyadema was France's man in the region for thirty-eight years, and Arlit's uranium fed French reactors. Guinea at 25 is the lowest, and it is 1958: Sekou Toure was the one African leader to vote non in de Gaulle's referendum, France withdrew everything down to the telephone wiring, and relations were not restored until 1975. Burkina Faso at 30 is the residue of Sankara, who had spent four years insulting Paris in public.",
+        "The Mali-Burkina Faso pair at 15 is a border war that ended. They fought in 1974 and again over five days at Christmas 1985; the International Court of Justice divided the Agacher Strip between them on 22 December 1986 and both accepted, which is why the roster carries no claim either way. What is left is 15 - correct, cool, and not friendly."
+      ],
+      "pairs": [
+        { "a": "Senegal", "b": "Mauritania", "value": -55.0 },
+        { "a": "Senegal", "b": "Gambia", "value": 35.0 },
+        { "a": "Senegal", "b": "GuineaBissau", "value": 20.0 },
+        { "a": "Senegal", "b": "Mali", "value": 35.0 },
+        { "a": "Senegal", "b": "Guinea", "value": 25.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "BurkinaFaso", "value": -45.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "Libya", "value": -50.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "USA", "value": 35.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "Israel", "value": 45.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "Nigeria", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "Guinea", "value": 15.0 },
+        { "a": "Liberia", "b": "SierraLeone", "value": 20.0 },
+        { "a": "Ghana", "b": "Togo", "value": -30.0 },
+        { "a": "Ghana", "b": "BurkinaFaso", "value": 15.0 },
+        { "a": "Mali", "b": "BurkinaFaso", "value": 15.0 },
+        { "a": "Mali", "b": "Algeria", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "Niger", "b": "Libya", "value": -15.0 },
+        { "a": "Niger", "b": "Nigeria", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "Benin", "b": "Nigeria", "value": 25.0 },
+        { "a": "Benin", "b": "Togo", "value": 15.0 },
+        { "a": "BurkinaFaso", "b": "Libya", "value": 45.0 },
+        { "a": "Guinea", "b": "SierraLeone", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "Guinea", "b": "GuineaBissau", "value": 25.0 },
+        { "a": "Mauritania", "b": "Morocco", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "Mauritania", "b": "Algeria", "value": 25.0 },
+        { "a": "Mauritania", "b": "Iraq", "value": 40.0 },
+        { "a": "Gambia", "b": "UK", "value": 55.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Togo", "value": 55.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Niger", "value": 55.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Mali", "value": 45.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Benin", "value": 35.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Mauritania", "value": 35.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "BurkinaFaso", "value": 30.0 },
+        { "a": "France", "b": "Guinea", "value": 25.0 },
+        { "a": "Portugal", "b": "GuineaBissau", "value": 35.0 }
+      ]
     }
   ]
 }
